{"theorems":[{"slogan_id":2424674,"theorem_id":18458194,"name":"Proposition 2.2 (limit distribution)","body":"Suppose $P$ is irreducible and reversible, and it has period 2. Then, $P$ has a unique even-time stationary distribution $\\mathring {\\pi }$, and $\\lim _{t \\to \\infty } \\mathring {x} P^{2t} = \\mathring {\\pi }$ for any even-time distribution $\\mathring {x}$.","slogan":"An irreducible and reversible Markov chain with period two has a unique stationary distribution for even times. The chain converges to this stationary distribution in the limit over even time steps. This convergence occurs from any initial even-time distribution.","theorem_type":"proposition","label":null,"link":null,"paper":{"paper_id":"2405.09102v1","source":"arXiv","title":"An Analysis of the Recurrence/Transience of Random Walks on Growing Trees and Hypercubes","authors":["Shuma Kumamoto","Shuji Kijima","Tomoyuki Shirai"],"link":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2405.09102v1","summary":null,"journal_ref":null,"primary_category":"math.PR","categories":["math.PR"],"citations":0,"year":2024,"journal_published":false},"similarity":0.6908455036054841,"score":0.6908455036054841,"has_metadata":true},{"slogan_id":1443278,"theorem_id":17464638,"name":"Theorem 1.3","body":"Let $X$ be a random walk on an $n$-cycle. If $n$ is even, the period of $X$ is 2. If $n$ is odd, $X$ is aperiodic.","slogan":"A random walk on an n-cycle has period 2 when n is even. When n is odd, the random walk is aperiodic.","theorem_type":"theorem","label":null,"link":null,"paper":{"paper_id":"2510.14165v1","source":"arXiv","title":"Finite Markov chains and Monte-Carlo Methods: An Undergraduate Introduction","authors":["Soumik Pal","Tim Mesikepp"],"link":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2510.14165v1","summary":null,"journal_ref":null,"primary_category":"math.PR","categories":["math.PR"],"citations":0,"year":2025,"journal_published":false},"similarity":0.6899858117103773,"score":0.6899858117103773,"has_metadata":true}]}